      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 8: a closed form for ε from route geometry",
      "text": "ε is predictable from grade alone on real descents: ε ≈ min(1, (α/β)/s̄) − ε₀ (unclamped since 2026-07-28 — the old clamp01 was provably inert on every measured ride), with ε₀ ≈ 0.13 the near-constant COASTING DEFICIT — the share of the descent pure coasting would refund but the rider does not collect, through residual descent pedalling and pre-corner braking; the remaining scatter is rider behaviour, not route geometry.",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
